# A forever loop as the last statement of an if/else arm terminates that arm.
function f takes number n returns number is
    if n is less than 0
        return -1
    else
        variable i is 0
        repeat forever
            add 1 to i
            if i is n
                return i
            end if
        end repeat
    end if
end function
constant a is the result of f -5
say a
constant b is the result of f 7
say b
